Description: CVE-2026-79020 - Fix out-of-bounds read in SkTiff::ImageFileDirectory::getEntryValuesGeneric
 getEntryValuesGeneric() validated the entry data size using the entry's own
 type (BytesForType(type) * count) but then iterated over the values with a
 fixed four-byte stride (BytesForType(kTypeUnsignedLong)). For two-byte
 values (SHORT) the stride overran the validated data, and for eight-byte
 values (RATIONAL) elements were read at the wrong offsets, allowing a crafted
 TIFF image to cause an out-of-bounds read. Use the size of the entry's own
 type as the stride so every read stays within the validated entry data.
Origin: other, https://issues.chromium.org/issues/514017820
Bug: https://webkitgtk.org/security/WSA-2026-0006.html
Author: Root.io Security <security@root.io>
Last-Update: 2026-10-06
---
--- a/Source/ThirdParty/skia/src/codec/SkTiffUtility.cpp
+++ b/Source/ThirdParty/skia/src/codec/SkTiffUtility.cpp
@@ -250,7 +250,9 @@
         return false;
     }
     for (uint32_t i = 0; i < count; ++i) {
-        const uint8_t* data = entryData + i * BytesForType(kTypeUnsignedLong);
+        // Advance by the size of the entry's own type. A fixed four-byte stride would read past
+        // the end of the validated entry data for two-byte values.
+        const uint8_t* data = entryData + i * BytesForType(type);
         switch (type) {
             case kTypeUnsignedShort:
                 reinterpret_cast<uint16_t*>(values)[i] =
